{
  "_meta": {
    "what": "Which class contexts are user-facing, and under what name.",
    "why": "The class-context records are research output. Some of them are notes the researching agent wrote to whoever curates next — a class whose display name is 'Data integrity issues in source list' or ends 'miscategorized in this group' is a finding about the source data, not a class a reader belongs to. Those are excluded from the build rather than filtered in the app, so nothing downstream has to know.",
    "name": "A short title for a slug whose authored name is a bucket label or a mouthful. These are browse rows under a Library family, so they have to read at a glance — 'First-generation H1 antihistamines with anticholinergic deliriant activity' does not. Anything in parentheses still splits off into the subtitle, so a qualifier worth keeping can be written into the override. Omit a slug to keep its authored name.",
    "membership": "A compound written up in one class's research file sometimes carries another class's id — 2C-B is tagged 'amphetamine-monoamine-releasers' with high confidence in the amphetamine file, and carries no class at all in the phenethylamine-psychedelics file where it belongs. So a membership is kept only when the substance's own resolved category agrees with the class's dominant one, or the pair is listed in `compatible_categories`. A category of 'Other' or none cannot disagree, so those are kept — which is the long tail, and the case the class card is most useful for. `keep` overrides a drop for a verified member."
  },
